en
  prompt
    templates
      agent-prompts
        buildUserPrompt
          text1 "Issue linked to PR #{{prNumber}}"
          text2 "Issue to solve: {{value1}}"
      ci-pre-existing-failure
        buildCiFailureGuidance
          text1 "Fix every failing check, including failures that also happen on the default branch: this pull request cannot be merged or released while its CI fails, whatever the cause."
          text2 "If a check can only pass after a human action you cannot do yourself (for example adding a secret, or granting access to a private repository or submodule), change the CI/CD configuration so that:"
          text3 "  - CI on this pull request passes without that action (for example, skip only the step that needs the missing secret or access, and print why it was skipped);"
          text4 "  - CI on the default branch fails with an explicit message that says exactly what a human has to do, so the job can be re-run and pass once that is done."
          text5 "Describe that manual action in the pull request description."
        buildPreExistingCiFeedback
          text6 "⚠️ These CI failures are pre-existing - they also fail without this pull request's changes:"
          text7 "That does not make them optional: they still block this pull request, so fix them here as described above."
      claude-prompts
        buildUserPrompt
          text1 "Continue the auto-restart from the previous resumed session."
          text2 "Issue linked to PR #{{prNumber}}"
          text3 "Issue to solve: {{value1}}"
          text4 "GitHub Actions on your fork: {{value1}}"
      codex-prompts
        buildUserPrompt
          text1 "Issue linked to PR #{{prNumber}}"
          text2 "Issue to solve: {{value1}}"
      deep-analysis
        buildDeepAnalysisPrompt
          text1 "Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the {{directory}} folder."
          text2 "Collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the {{directory}} folder."
          text3 "Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help."
          text4 "If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off."
          text5 "If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code."
          text6 "Do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), list each and every requirement from the issue, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help."
          text7 "Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them."
      development-log
        buildDevelopmentLogPrompt
          text1 "Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data into the {{developmentLogDirectory}} folder."
          text2 "Collect data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data into the {{developmentLogDirectory}} folder."
      fix-ci-cd
        buildLanguagesSection
          text1 "No languages were reported by the GitHub Linguist API for this repository."
        buildTemplatesSection
          text2 "No language-specific template matched the detected languages. Review all templates and apply the closest match:"
          text3 "Apply the best practices from these templates, in priority order (most-used language first):"
          text4 "Other detected languages without a dedicated template: {{value1}}."
        buildRunsSection
          text5 "No CI/CD runs were found for the latest default-branch commit."
          text6 """
            | Workflow | Status | Conclusion | Commit | Run |
            | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
          """
          text7 """
            | Workflow | Status | Conclusion | Run |
            | --- | --- | --- | --- |
          """
        buildCiCdIssueBody
          text13 "default branch"
          text14 "Recent CI/CD runs on `{{value1}}`"
          text15 "Latest default-branch CI/CD runs"
          text16 "the default branch"
          text17 "No recent CI/CD runs were found on `{{value1}}`."
          text18 "No CI/CD runs were found for the latest default-branch commit."
          text19 "<summary>Context collected by <code>/fix --ci-cd</code></summary>"
          text20 "- **Default branch:** `{{value1}}`"
          text21 "- **Latest commit:** {{commitLine}}"
          text22 "- **CI/CD runs found:** {{total}} ({{failing}} not passing)"
          text23 "**Detected languages**"
          text24 "**Recommended CI/CD templates**"
        DEBUG_OUTPUT_PARAGRAPH
          text8 "If there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration."
        REPORT_UPSTREAM_PARAGRAPH
          text9 "If issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them."
        buildStandardPromptParagraphs
          text10 """
            Use all the best practices from CI/CD templates (check full file tree to compare for all GitHub workflow and CI/CD scripts file), if the same issue is found in template report issue also in templates:

            {{templateLinks}}
          """
          text11 "We should compare all files, so we don't have more CI/CD errors in the future and reuse all the best practices from these templates."
          text12 "Follow the CI/CD best practices collected in [{{CI_CD_BEST_PRACTICES_URL}}]({{CI_CD_BEST_PRACTICES_URL}})."
      fix-update-dependencies
        buildEcosystemsSection
          text1 "No package ecosystem was detected automatically. Inspect the repository for dependency manifests by hand and update every one of them."
          text2 "Update **every** ecosystem below, in this order (most of the repository first). One pull request may cover them all, but each ecosystem must end up fully current — not partially."
          text3 "   - Detected languages: {{value1}}"
          text4 "_none found — check whether one is missing_"
          text5 "   - Manifests: {{value1}}"
          text6 "   - Lockfiles to regenerate and commit: {{value1}}"
          text7 "   - Update everything: {{value1}}"
          text8 "Detected languages with no dependency manifest of their own: {{value1}}. Check whether they pull dependencies through one of the ecosystems above."
        buildAutomationSection
          text9 "`.github/dependabot.yml` already exists — verify it covers every ecosystem and directory listed above, then keep it in sync with any manifest this work adds or moves."
          text10 "There is no `.github/dependabot.yml` in this repository, so nothing keeps the versions current after this issue is closed. Add one so the next drift is a pull request instead of another issue."
          text11 "The ecosystems found in this repository correspond to these entries:"
          text12 "For the ecosystems found in this repository that is:"
          text13 "Only the first {{MAX_DEPENDABOT_DIRECTORIES}} directories are listed per ecosystem — add the remaining ones, or replace the list with a glob (`directories` supports `*`; `directory` does not)."
          text14 "[Renovate](https://docs.renovatebot.com/) is the alternative if grouped or automerged updates are wanted instead."
        buildUpdateDependenciesIssueBody
          text25 "### Dependency ecosystems detected in this repository"
          text26 "### Keeping them current"
          text27 "<summary>Context collected by <code>/fix --update-all-dependencies</code></summary>"
          text28 "- **Default branch:** `{{value1}}`"
          text29 "- **Latest commit:** {{commitLine}}"
          text30 "- **Ecosystems detected:** {{value1}}"
          text31 "- **Manifest files found:** {{value1}}"
          text32 "- ⚠️ **The file listing returned by GitHub was truncated**, so the manifest inventory above may be incomplete. Re-check the repository tree by hand."
          text33 "**Detected languages**"
